Since April, reports about dates landing on the wrong day were merged into ticket #4471.
The export contains three distinguishable problems, not one.

<SplitTable />

## What the split means

- **Parser:** the shared parser reads month first, while the tenant writes day first.
- **Hint:** the booking-v3 form shows month first, but the form reads it day first. This
  requires a different fix from the shared parser.
- **One-day move:** the desk notes describe reports with a one-day shift. They support
  treating these separately, but do not establish the underlying mechanism.

The current KB rule folds the one-day-move reports into the parser group. Some additional
reports have no date pair in their body; those are assigned by tenant and form rule, and
are not counted as clean body-proven swaps.

The published projection omits report subjects, report bodies, and tenant names. Tenant
keys are pseudonymous; counts and date ranges are computed from the sanitized records.

